WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:06.220
Marvel's ABC TV series Inhumans has made its
long-awaited debut, with a modified version

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.020
of the first two episodes landing in IMAX
theaters across the country.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.500
Unfortunately, the reaction from critics and
fans has not been kind.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.029
The theatrical release currently has yet to
earn a single positive review on Rotten Tomatoes,

00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:22.080
the box office take has been anemic, and fans
have been left wondering how a project that

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.470
spent such a long time in development is turning
out to be Marvel's first massive flop.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.239
There are several factors that brought Inhumans
to this point, so let's take a look at where

00:00:31.239 --> 00:00:33.820
this project went so wrong.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.340
Red light, green light

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:41.110
Inhumans was first announced in 2014, as part
of Marvel Studios' slate of then-upcoming

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:46.000
theatrical releases, and it was intended at
that time to be included in Phase Three.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.960
The Inhuman Royal Family was never the most
high-profile of Marvel's stable of characters.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.330
But at the time of the announcement, the studio
was coming off the surprise smash hit Guardians

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:59.760
of the Galaxy, featuring an ensemble of characters
whose profiles had previously been even lower.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:05.550
There seemed to be no reason for concern — until
April 2016, when the project was pulled from

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:06.920
Marvel's schedule.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.830
At first, Marvel Studios head honcho Kevin
Feige said the release date was just being

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:15.140
shuffled to make room for a solo Spider-Man
movie and a sequel to Ant-Man.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.990
But then the project moved to the small screen
with ABC, and things got even weirder.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:24.530
"We've been hiding here for too long, let's
go to our rightful home"

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:29.200
Rumors persisted that the project was in danger
of being scrapped altogether, and many fans

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:34.060
were surprised when casting announcements
soon began to hit the web — and then disappointed,

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.100
once teaser images soon followed.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.060
Terrible teasers

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:43.450
The Inhuman Royal Family consists of some
of the most colorful and outlandish characters

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.740
in Marvel Comics.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:50.050
You've got Medusa's swirling, deadly red locks
and Gorgon's sci-fi-fantasy aesthetic and

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:51.140
the fish-man Triton.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.630
So, the series' visual design calls for some
serious artistic flair.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:59.760
But when the first teaser images of the cast
in costume were released, it quickly became

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.790
apparent that we were not going to get that.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.590
Fans immediately voiced their dismay on social
media.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:09.770
Medusa in particular was singled out, as her
hair was less of a special effect and more

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.020
of a really bad wig.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:15.780
The bargain-basement feel of the crucial first
promotional image didn't do anything to increase

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:19.170
their anticipation of what should've been
a visual spectacle.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.819
And the trailers weren't much better.

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:25.930
Despite an appearance by the teleporting dog
Lockjaw getting a positive response, pretty

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:30.200
much every other aspect of the trailer was
widely criticized.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:35.170
Medusa again underwhelmed as fans got not
even a tease of what her hair could do, and

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.770
some even began to wonder if her abilities
would make it into the show at all.

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:43.540
The second trailer resolved that issue — but
only by employing some of the worst CGI effects

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.420
this side of a ten year-old SyFy movie.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:47.420
"Never."

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:53.340
A preview shown at San Diego Comic-Con also
left fans deriding the new footage as "aggressively

00:02:53.349 --> 00:02:54.349
awful."

00:02:54.349 --> 00:02:58.349
So, instead of hype, the imagery only earned
gripes.

00:02:58.349 --> 00:03:00.120
Awkward press panel

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:05.350
A few weeks prior to the release of the IMAX
presentation, ABC TV held its annual press

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.879
event with the Television Critics' Association.

00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:11.790
When the cast of Inhumans came out to talk
to the assembled journalists, it became quickly

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:15.910
apparent that they may not have been ready
to field question after question about the

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:21.099
poor internet reaction to the trailers and
the show's perceived lack of quality.

00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:25.380
Anson Mount, for example, responded to questions
about the poor reception by saying they made

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:28.720
him feel like Ben Affleck during the Batman
Vs. Superman tour.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:34.320
"I agree."

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.440
And the rest of the cast members were viewed
as evasive, deflective, and somewhat bewildered

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.410
by what they were up against.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:46.110
Marvel TV chief Jeph Loeb even snapped at
reporters and shut the event down early.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:49.870
Of course, the cast may have had a reason
to be on edge.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.650
Imperiled production

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:55.900
The plan to divert Inhumans from the silver
to small screen meant that producers had just

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:01.750
months to cast, write, and develop an eight-episode
miniseries from an already ambitious basis.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:06.209
Making matters worse, the IMAX premiere of
the first two episodes meant that those episodes

00:04:06.209 --> 00:04:09.519
would have to be produced on an extremely
accelerated schedule.

00:04:09.519 --> 00:04:13.790
Those episodes' director, Roel Reine, revealed
that although the process was "collaborative,"

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:18.090
he was definitely under the studio's thumb
all the while, telling CNET, there was "always

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:22.410
a Marvel executive around me just to make
sure that whatever I did, or whatever we did

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:27.560
together, would tie in with other characters
in other universes, in other comics, in other

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.200
series or movies.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.380
They're very protective."

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.110
The rushed nature of the production is apparent
in the finished product, and the fact that

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:40.400
some scenes are gorgeously shot in IMAX actually
hurts rather than helps.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.590
The IMAX experiment

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:46.770
Critics have pointed out that the scenes that
are shot in IMAX look fantastic, but that

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:50.000
they also make it even more apparent which
scenes were not.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.530
The interiors and costumes have every bit
the low-budget aesthetic suggested by the

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.960
trailers, flaws that are only magnified up
on that gigantic screen, with the gorgeous

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:04.130
IMAX footage occasionally popping in to make
the rest of the film look even worse by comparison.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.450
"We're inhumans"

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:10.530
In the first week of a planned two-week run,
Inhumans grossed about $1.5 million, which

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.009
is a paltry sum compared to the promotional
expenses.

00:05:13.009 --> 00:05:18.110
While an investment by IMAX will make Inhumans
profitable for Disney no matter what happens,

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:23.170
it's not exactly encouraging for partnerships
of this kind in the future.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.690
Critical miss

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:29.960
In the summer of flailing film studios blaming
critics for killing their box office returns,

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:31.860
Inhumans is no exception.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:36.380
Reviewers overwhelmingly railed on what they
saw in the series, from the acting to direction

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:39.630
to set design and even special effects.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:43.040
Some have gone so far as to call it the worst
thing Marvel has done.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:48.169
And after the critical lashing the Marvel
TV execs took for Iron Fist, that says a lot.

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:51.770
Perhaps the fact that the studio gave the
reins of the show to Iron Fist's showrunner

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:55.520
Scott Buck can be blamed for that double-dose
of disses.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:59.920
After all, Iron Fist also failed to live up
to expectations for similar reasons.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:04.610
Both shows were rushed in conception and execution,
poorly written and plotted, and indifferently

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:06.100
staged and photographed.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:09.789
Whether or not the failure of Inhumans is
part of any trend of declining quality among

00:06:09.789 --> 00:06:14.789
Marvel TV productions is up for debate, but
if Buck is allowed to go to bat for a third

00:06:14.789 --> 00:06:18.580
Marvel property, he's going to have two strikes
against him already.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:19.580
Thanks for watching!

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:21.960
